1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,640
NextView: an agent that calibrates a camera by

2
00:00:03,660 --> 00:00:06,470
deciding where the calibration board should go next.

3
00:00:07,533 --> 00:00:09,793
A solo entry by Umar Mohktar, Singapore:

4
00:00:10,453 --> 00:00:12,963
design, implementation and evaluation.

5
00:00:14,167 --> 00:00:17,187
Calibration is step zero of every metric inspection,

6
00:00:17,207 --> 00:00:19,307
and its usual check misleads.

7
00:00:19,847 --> 00:00:20,807
After a few views,

8
00:00:21,087 --> 00:00:23,587
the in-sample error is under a tenth of a pixel,

9
00:00:23,767 --> 00:00:26,957
while the true error at the image edges is many pixels.

10
00:00:27,433 --> 00:00:29,173
This is the live app on AWS.

11
00:00:29,773 --> 00:00:32,983
The camera is simulated, so the true error is known.

12
00:00:33,201 --> 00:00:35,241
Each step checks the frame and rejects

13
00:00:35,261 --> 00:00:37,121
bad ones with a measured reason,

14
00:00:37,441 --> 00:00:40,121
such as blur in pixels on the board's own edges,

15
00:00:40,501 --> 00:00:43,811
then gives a numeric instruction and a ghost outline.

16
00:00:43,997 --> 00:00:45,897
Candidate poses are ranked by the

17
00:00:45,917 --> 00:00:47,437
predicted drop in uncertainty,

18
00:00:47,837 --> 00:00:49,483
and each capture reports what it actually achieved.

19
00:00:49,533 --> 00:00:51,573
When the residuals show a radial trend,

20
00:00:51,933 --> 00:00:54,513
the agent asks before it changes the lens model.

21
00:00:55,053 --> 00:00:58,383
Deny, and the model stays pinned while the plan continues.

22
00:01:01,833 --> 00:01:03,483
Restart with the same seed.

23
00:01:09,644 --> 00:01:11,383
This time, approve, and it refits with the rational model.

24
00:01:11,433 --> 00:01:13,553
The race chart compares the true error with

25
00:01:13,573 --> 00:01:15,573
random poses on the same camera.

26
00:01:16,113 --> 00:01:19,773
It is one session, and the baseline keeps the k5 lens model,

27
00:01:20,013 --> 00:01:22,283
so part of the gap is the model switch.

28
00:01:22,550 --> 00:01:24,330
It stops when the calibrated chance of

29
00:01:24,350 --> 00:01:28,570
exceeding 0.75 pixels drops below ten percent.

30
00:01:29,430 --> 00:01:32,930
Export needs approval too, and returns OpenCV YAML,

31
00:01:33,210 --> 00:01:35,660
a report card and a JSON record.

32
00:01:36,733 --> 00:01:39,993
The webcam tab runs the same agent on browser frames;

33
00:01:40,473 --> 00:01:43,393
here, a virtual camera plays a rendered board video.

34
00:01:43,973 --> 00:01:45,403
Frames are never stored.

35
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:54,000
It runs as one stateless Lambda container behind API Gateway,

36
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:56,340
with session state in a signed token.

37
00:01:57,180 --> 00:02:00,860
Traces go to CloudWatch, approved exports to private S3,

38
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:04,870
and a median step takes 1.4 seconds on the server.

39
00:02:06,133 --> 00:02:08,073
The Evidence tab serves the benchmark's

40
00:02:08,093 --> 00:02:09,633
figures and headline numbers,

41
00:02:09,653 --> 00:02:11,823
baked into the deployed image.

42
00:02:13,033 --> 00:02:16,353
In a pre-registered benchmark on 100 simulated test cameras,

43
00:02:16,733 --> 00:02:19,013
all eight primary endpoints favour the agent.

44
00:02:19,693 --> 00:02:23,753
After ten frames, the median true error is 1.21 pixels

45
00:02:24,293 --> 00:02:27,673
against 2.71 for random poses with a robot,

46
00:02:28,093 --> 00:02:31,963
and 1.22 against 3.61 with a human.

47
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:35,260
The agent gets below one pixel in a

48
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:37,440
median of 8 frames with a robot;

49
00:02:38,020 --> 00:02:41,230
the median random-pose run does not get there within 30.

50
00:02:42,267 --> 00:02:43,967
Taking parts out one at a time:

51
00:02:44,327 --> 00:02:46,227
the planner, outlier dropping and,

52
00:02:46,247 --> 00:02:48,787
on wide lenses, the model switch all help.

53
00:02:49,327 --> 00:02:51,227
The perception gate adds no accuracy,

54
00:02:51,247 --> 00:02:54,697
and costs a human 18 attempts instead of 10.

55
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:57,540
The uncertainty map is optimistic,

56
00:02:57,940 --> 00:03:00,800
so the stop rule is calibrated on separate cameras.

57
00:03:01,480 --> 00:03:06,740
190 of 300 robot runs stopped, none above 1.5 pixels,

58
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:09,310
but telephoto runs never stopped.

59
00:03:10,333 --> 00:03:13,653
On real D455 images from the METRIC dataset,

60
00:03:14,153 --> 00:03:16,013
the agent is not consistently better

61
00:03:16,033 --> 00:03:18,313
than random frame choices:

62
00:03:18,333 --> 00:03:20,413
it ranks between the 2nd and 84th

63
00:03:20,433 --> 00:03:23,083
percentile of 100 random draws.

64
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:27,300
At one metre, a 100 mm segment near the image edge is

65
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:30,980
off by a median 0.047 mm after ten frames,

66
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:35,840
against 0.12 to 0.17 mm for random poses.

67
00:03:35,860 --> 00:03:40,180
On wide lenses, though, before the lens-model switch,

68
00:03:40,620 --> 00:03:42,100
the agent's worst segments near the

69
00:03:42,120 --> 00:03:45,060
corners are off by 25.9 mm,

70
00:03:45,300 --> 00:03:47,970
against 5.7 mm for a dense grid.

71
00:03:48,933 --> 00:03:54,513
Over MCP, a local Qwen 2.5 7B model drove the same tools:

72
00:03:55,093 --> 00:03:56,533
10 of 10 sessions finished,

73
00:03:56,893 --> 00:03:59,033
98 percent of calls were valid,

74
00:03:59,053 --> 00:04:00,703
and its error matched the planner's.

75
00:04:01,833 --> 00:04:04,953
Failures are evidence too: across 60 fisheye,

76
00:04:05,113 --> 00:04:07,413
autofocus-drift and warped-board runs,

77
00:04:07,713 --> 00:04:09,843
the agent never issued a clean stop.

78
00:04:10,933 --> 00:04:14,173
NextView is decision support, not certified metrology.

79
00:04:14,953 --> 00:04:16,833
Primary results are simulator-graded,

80
00:04:17,273 --> 00:04:18,933
webcam frames are never stored,

81
00:04:19,233 --> 00:04:21,183
and the trace is the audit record.
